1490
01:04:11.020 --> 01:04:11.560
I know.

1491
01:04:11.640 --> 01:04:12.300
So good.

1492
01:04:12.680 --> 01:04:14.880
We're all just staring at him.

1493
01:04:15.040 --> 01:04:17.260
And Ed played the moment so perfectly.

1494
01:04:17.720 --> 01:04:20.280
My heart completely broke for Andy.

1495
01:04:20.340 --> 01:04:23.840
I felt so bad for him and I started to cry.

1496
01:04:24.060 --> 01:04:25.400
Like actually crying?

1497
01:04:25.660 --> 01:04:25.900
Yeah.

1498
01:04:26.380 --> 01:04:27.940
I actually cry.

1499
01:04:28.100 --> 01:04:33.600
If you look at this, it pushes it on my face and I'm completely tearing up.

1500
01:04:33.600 --> 01:04:45.060
Those are those moments as an actor where you have so inhabited your character's story and the story of the people around you where your body,

1501
01:04:45.260 --> 01:04:48.680
like you didn't even have to make yourself cry or think of something sad.

1502
01:04:48.680 --> 01:04:52.780
You were just so in the moment that the emotions just flood.

1503
01:04:53.060 --> 01:04:54.360
No, really, really.

1504
01:04:54.500 --> 01:04:56.900
And everyone was playing it so real.

1505
01:04:57.540 --> 01:04:59.100
Paul Feig told us to.

1506
01:04:59.320 --> 01:05:05.560
Like he said when we come around with that B camera, and this was similar to his direction in Office Olympics, he said,

1507
01:05:05.740 --> 01:05:10.400
I don't want you to comment on it with no kind of funny looks or anything.

1508
01:05:10.720 --> 01:05:14.600
Like this is like truly a human moment.

1509
01:05:14.940 --> 01:05:16.360
And just stand there.

1510
01:05:16.540 --> 01:05:17.800
Just be in it.

1511
01:05:18.280 --> 01:05:19.700
It was great direction.

1512
01:05:20.120 --> 01:05:21.180
And you felt it.

1513
01:05:21.300 --> 01:05:21.540
Yeah.

1514
01:05:21.860 --> 01:05:22.880
It felt heavy.

1515
01:05:23.140 --> 01:05:24.200
It felt really heavy.

1516
01:05:24.200 --> 01:05:26.560
And I felt horrible.

1517
01:05:27.220 --> 01:05:28.720
And I started to cry.

1518
01:05:29.300 --> 01:05:37.480
You know, in re-watching it all, I just thought this episode was written and directed and acted so, so well.

1519
01:05:37.660 --> 01:05:39.280
I was really proud of us as a show.

1520
01:05:39.460 --> 01:05:40.480
You know what, Angela?

1521
01:05:40.720 --> 01:05:43.400
This was what Paul Feig could do for us.

1522
01:05:43.620 --> 01:05:51.420
